From cc9e4da5e9b1dee25797664e6b919222821ff3f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:50:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] Archive verified ancestry headers so a missed root
 recovers with every upstream down

On P's authenticated ancestry (7b4dd692) with the S3 archive tier:

* witness-gateway: a header that ancestry recovery verified (helper op
  `header`, hash and child binding) is queued for the archive, never
  awaited, keyed by its own block hash. When every upstream fails to give a
  header, archived candidates are checked by the same helper call and
  quarantined like witnesses. Roots still come only from a signed head and
  hash links below it: no signed head = nothing recovered, a block above the
  newest signed head is refused, and the archive is never a root or freshness
  authority. The archive read/put helpers are shared with the witness path.
* tests (REAL checker, MinIO): real Base headers 52965055..106 under the real
  signer (header binding only, no proofs) recovered from the archive with the
  upstream down; first-sorting forged headers quarantined; a missing link or a
  header filed under another hash refused; no head / older head / wrong
  signer refused; real proofs at a recovered root under SYNTHETIC authority
  (P's labelled 249'/250' fixture) served archive-only with forged first
  header and proof quarantined; hung/unavailable S3 neither delays recovery
  nor outlives its deadline, close() reaps every child. Helios E2E: cold
  ancestry from the archive only (synthetic authority).
* s3-test-env: a MinIO that never becomes ready is an explicit test-env
  error, not a later 503.

(cherry picked from commit afc443e032647c2d8ea31535f5ff0f6609d99ba6)
